  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nStep 5 of the [focusing steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#focusing-steps) returns early when \"new focus target is the [currently focused area of a top-level traversable](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#currently-focused-area-of-a-top-level-traversable)\". But that algorithm starts with \"If *traversable* does not have system focus, then return null\", so in a window or tab without system focus, the check never matches.\n\nAs a result, calling `focus()` on the element that already has focus runs the focus update steps again in that case.\n\nWeb engines don't do that, they don't depend on system focus here, they compare against the document's focused element.\n\nI guess the spec needs to be updated to match that web engines do in this case.\n",
